      "standard_id": "EFO",
      "name": "Experimental Factor Ontology (EFO)",
      "description": "A data-driven biomedical ontology used to represent experimental variables and sample attributes (traits, diseases, anatomical and cell types, experimental factors). Used for annotation, curation, query and visualization across resources (e.g. Gene Expression Atlas, NHGRI-EBI GWAS Catalog, BioSamples) and mapped to other resources such as Ensembl variation; functions as a metadata/ontology standard for describing samples and phenotypes."
    }
